.TH FL-DOCS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-docs \- PDF viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-docs\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fIFILE.pdf\fR]
.br
\fBfl-docs \-\-info\fR \fIFILE.pdf\fR [\fB\-\-find\fR \fITEXT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows PDF documents (through poppler) in one continuously scrolling strip of
pages, with page thumbnails on the left. The zoom fits the width (of the
widest page) or the whole page, or is set from 10% to 800%. Search finds a
text on all pages, without regard to case, and highlights every match.
Printing goes to a CUPS printer with copies, a page range and two-sided
printing. Documents protected by a password ask for it. A PDF dropped onto
the window opens.
.SH KEYS
.TP
Ctrl+O, Ctrl+P
Open, print.
.TP
Ctrl+F, Enter, F3, Shift+F3
Find; the next and the previous match.
.TP
Page Up, Page Down, Space, arrows, Home, End, N, P
Scroll; first and last page; next and previous page.
.TP
Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus, Ctrl+0, Ctrl+wheel
Zoom in, out, to 100%.
.TP
F9
Show or hide the thumbnails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR
Open at page \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-info\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-find\fR \fITEXT\fR]
Print the number of pages, the title and the page sizes in points and, with
\fB\-\-find\fR, every match as "hit PAGE X Y WIDTH HEIGHT" (points from the
top left corner), without opening a window.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-printers\fR(1), \fBfl-view\fR(1)
